@startuml lockfree-structural-sharing
' ============================================================================
' lockfree-structural-sharing.puml — a persistent (immutable) key vector shares
' its interior with the new version on insert: appending 'x' copies only the
' O(log n) tree nodes on the touched path; every other interior node is shared
' by Arc, and the old version is left completely unchanged (both coexist).
' Source: §Structural Sharing with im::Vector of lockfree-cas-artrie.md.
' NOTE: the byte overlay has since replaced im::Vector with a tiered ChildStore
' (Inline ≤4 / Heap 5+); this figure illustrates the persistent-vector PRINCIPLE.
' Color key (house palette):
'   green  #C8E6C9  interior nodes SHARED between both versions (no copy)
'   teal   #B2DFDB  the O(log n) path copied for the new version + the new leaf
'   grey   #ECEFF1  version labels
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #212121
  BorderThickness 1.3
}

title Structural sharing — insert('x') copies only the O(log n) touched path

rectangle "**v0** root\n(old version)" as R0 #ECEFF1
rectangle "**v1** root\n(after insert 'x')" as R1 #B2DFDB

package "shared interior (both roots — no copy)" #F1F8F4 {
  rectangle "interior\n[a b c d]" as I1 #C8E6C9
  rectangle "interior\n[e f g h]" as I2 #C8E6C9
}

package "copied for v1 — O(log n) nodes" #E0F2F1 {
  rectangle "copied interior\n[… + x]" as I3 #B2DFDB
  rectangle "new leaf 'x'" as LX #B2DFDB
}

R0 -down-> I1
R0 -down-> I2
R1 -[#2E7D32,bold]-> I1 : shared
R1 -down-> I3
I3 -[#2E7D32,bold]-> I2 : shared
I3 -down-> LX

note bottom of LX
  v0 is UNCHANGED — both versions coexist.
  Only the root→slot spine is reallocated
  (O(log n)); all other subtrees are shared.
end note
@enduml
